{%- comment -%}
  Shop by Strength Product Line — packaging-video CTA on the PDP "Ships" row.

  Remediation per Tim French, thread "Update needed — Shop by Strength Product
  Line shipping block / packaging video" (2026-07-17 and 2026-07-21 reviews).

    1. No hardcoded SKU/handle exclusion list. Suppression is driven by controlled
       product data: the boolean metafield custom.packaging_video_exception.
       Rule: every product in the "shop-by-strength-product-line" collection shows
       the CTA UNLESS it carries an approved, documented exception (metafield == true).

    2. CTA text is "Watch Packaging Example".

    3. CTA is a real link to the packaging video that opens in a new tab with
       target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer".

    4. Video URL is read from the controlled product metafield custom.watch_packaging_video,
       with a single theme-level fallback defined ONCE here (not repeated across the three
       PDP sections: main-product, main-product-comb, main-product-variants).

    5. Representative-example disclaimer: the approved generic copy is defined ONCE here as
       the shared fallback, so it does not have to be populated on ~239 products. The
       metafield custom.packaging_disclaimer is an OPTIONAL per-product override. The
       disclaimer is presented through a native <details>/<summary> disclosure, which is
       touch- and keyboard-accessible without JS (not a title-only tooltip).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign in_strength_line = false
  for collection in product.collections
    if collection.handle contains 'shop-by-strength-product-line'
      assign in_strength_line = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign is_exception = false
  if product.metafields.custom.packaging_video_exception.value == true
    assign is_exception = true
  endif

  assign show_packaging_video = false
  if in_strength_line and is_exception == false
    assign show_packaging_video = true
  endif

  assign packaging_video_url = product.metafields.custom.watch_packaging_video.value
  if packaging_video_url == blank
    assign packaging_video_url = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/ac6b9c86a3c741059abf9f9fd23b51ec.mp4'
  endif

  assign packaging_disclaimer = product.metafields.custom.packaging_disclaimer.value
  if packaging_disclaimer == blank
    assign packaging_disclaimer = 'All French Fitness strength product-line equipment receives protective blanket wrapping for freight transit. Depending on the model and shipment, primary packaging may also include manufacturer cartons, a pallet or wood frame, and/or a wooden crate. Some components or hardware may arrive pre-installed for transport and assembly. This video shows a representative packaging example; exact packaging may vary by model and shipment.'
  endif
-%}
{%- if show_packaging_video -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Keep the "—" separator OUTSIDE the link. The anchor is underlined/clickable, so a
    dash inside it would look like part of the link (per the main-branch fix that moved
    the dash out of the old .more-info span).

    The inline dash/link lives in a <span>; the block-level <details> disclosure is a
    SIBLING of that span (not nested inside it) so the markup is valid. Dynamic values
    are escaped: the href via `escape`, and the optional disclaimer override via
    `escape | newline_to_br` so admin-entered text cannot be interpreted as markup while
    line breaks are preserved.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="packaging-video">
    —
    <a
      class="packaging-video__link"
      href="{{ packaging_video_url | escape }}"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >Watch Packaging Example</a>
  </span>
  <details class="packaging-video__details">
    <summary class="packaging-video__summary">Packaging details <span class="packaging-video__caret" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'icon-caret' %}</span></summary>
    <span class="packaging-video__disclaimer">{{ packaging_disclaimer | escape | newline_to_br }}</span>
  </details>
  {%- comment -%}
    The theme-wide `summary` reset in base.css.liquid removes the native disclosure
    marker (list-style: none + hidden ::-webkit-details-marker), so add a visible caret
    affordance using the theme's icon-caret snippet (styled by the existing
    `summary .icon-caret` rule) and rotate it on [open] to signal expanded/collapsed state.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>
    .packaging-video__caret {
      display: inline-flex;
      vertical-align: middle;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease;
    }
    .packaging-video__details[open] .packaging-video__caret {
      transform: rotate(180deg);
    }
    .packaging-video__link,
    .packaging-video__summary {
      text-decoration: underline;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
